## On pull requests

| Workflow | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ci.yml` (Server Tests) | Skips PRs that only touch css/js/md/html/csv. Brings up a bench through `.github/helper/install.sh`: frappe and erpnext on the **same branch name as the PR base**, plus the payments app, MariaDB 11.8 and Python 3.14. Then it runs `bench run-parallel-tests --app healthcare`. It also runs nightly at 00:00 UTC; nightly runs upload coverage to Codecov. |
| `linters.yml` / `linters.v2.yml` | pre-commit (ruff, ruff-format, prettier, eslint, detect-secrets, pip-audit, file checks) and Semgrep with the Frappe rules plus `r/python.lang.correctness`. |
| `semantic-commits.yml` | commitlint over the PR's commits. |
| `docs_checker.yml` | `feat` PRs need a wiki docs link (or `no-docs`). |
| `labeller.yml` | Adds the `needs-tests` label. |
| `codeql.yml` | CodeQL for Python and JS on `develop` and weekly. |

The default branch of this fork is `biograph-fh`. Several workflows still reference upstream `earthians/biograph` and its `develop` / `version-*` branches.

## Release (upstream model)

- **Weekly** (Tuesday 09:30 UTC), `initiate_release.yml` opens `version-NN-hotfix → version-NN` PRs for 14, 15 and 16.
- When a `version-*` branch receives a push, `on_release.yml` runs **semantic-release** (`.releaserc`, angular preset; breaking changes do not trigger a major release). It rewrites the version in `healthcare/__init__.py`, commits `chore(release): Bumped to Version x.y.z`, and publishes a GitHub release.
- `release_notes.yml` regenerates release notes and strips chore/ci/test/docs/style entries. PRs labelled `skip-release-notes` are excluded (`.github/release.yml`).
- `generate-pot-file.yml` regenerates `main.pot` every week. Crowdin opens `fix: sync translations from crowdin` PRs.
- Dependabot updates GitHub Actions weekly.

There is no deploy step. Users install the app onto Frappe benches (Frappe Cloud or self-hosted) with `bench get-app` and `bench migrate`.
